    "new-round/sqrt_two_irrational": {
      "scope": "statement and parity proof",
      "text": "sqrt(2) is irrational. Otherwise write sqrt(2) = p/q in lowest terms, with p an integer and q a positive integer. Squaring gives p^2 = 2q^2, so p is even. Write p = 2k; then q^2 = 2k^2, so q is even too. This contradicts gcd(p,q) = 1.",
      "informal_characters": 188,
